A sustained book and graduate-course programme (@fd-whole-books: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG", #fluid-dynamics "../research/Advanced-hydrostatic-load-and-inverse-density-study.lingua#r_4ANS8VPM2VV66Y3FVSW7TZ5SDJ") { r_4P4AF2QKRVED55XXYWDRFD47B3
**Read:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG), the edition, access and scope notes for every sustained reading.

Work a complete introductory fluid text rather than replacing it with these connecting explanations. Read all of [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18) and use all eight chapters of [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J) for the Portuguese mathematical and physical account. Complete the relevant mechanics preparation from [University Physics Volume 1 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-1.lingua#r_2W7QCEHZ45XDB3AWVG9NTV36F6) and the public introductory engineering progression. Keep derivations, solved unfamiliar problems and physical observations together as the quantities acquire meaning.

Then work all eleven chapters of [Intermediate Fluid Mechanics — James Liburdy](../sources/Intermediate-Fluid-Mechanics-Liburdy.lingua#r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N), the six PDF chapters of [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), and the full analytical development in [Fluid Mechanics — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Analytical-Fluid-Mechanics-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_075CGXNA8WHV26ZW53C7XTQ48V) with its mathematical appendices. Use the available [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ) problems and examinations as independent challenges, including cases whose method is not stated in advance. The public material is a study resource; it does not confer the institution's assessment or qualification.

Continue through the complete turbulence, multiphase, cavitation and non-Newtonian readings, selected complete Mei modules, the interfacial course, and the full computational and experimental programmes as their questions arise. [Gas Dynamics — Vinayak Kulkarni](../sources/Gas-Dynamics-Kulkarni.lingua#r_34YGDV61X77JFYZH8X8NGDBS9W) and [Advanced Hydraulics — Suresh A. Kartha](../sources/Advanced-Hydraulics-Kartha.lingua#r_1MCV024RY5CA95WTHY708FP7VT) deepen compressible and free-surface work. A complete book supplies a coherent argument; the following investigations require putting that argument to work, testing it and comparing it with primary evidence.

**Continue:** [Advanced hydrostatic load and inverse-density study](../research/Advanced-hydrostatic-load-and-inverse-density-study.lingua#r_4ANS8VPM2VV66Y3FVSW7TZ5SDJ).

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics — motion, forces, transport and evidence](../Fluid-dynamics.lingua#r_7PQW1WDHK708BFV23MD8ET61VZ).
} r_4P4AF2QKRVED55XXYWDRFD47B3
